    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174-a3">

                <pb facs="0368" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg312"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    219.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of circular No</hi>. 4064, 4209.</head>
                <p>Subject: On the suppression of some books in the schools.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kingdom of Greece</hi>.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">The ministry of ecclesiastical affairs and public instruction
                    to the prefects and subprefects of the kingdom:</p>
                <p>Inclosing herewith sufficient copies of the circular issued to-day to the
                    directors of the communal or private male and female schools, we invite you to
                    send a copy to each one of these directors who may be in your district. At the
                    same time we call your strict attention to what is therein prescribed; to attend
                    to the execution of what is ordered by the above-mentioned circular, and also
                    prevent the selling and circulation of such books; keeping in that way the
                    simplest of citizens from the trap which is laid against their piety.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19th, / <hi
                                rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1, 1876</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> The minister,<lb/><signed>G. MILISSIS.</signed><lb/>The
                            secretary,<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alex. I. V.
                            Vlachos</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
